  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Transactions and the ACID Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Transactions and the ACID Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Transaction Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==transaction== = a group of statements run as **one all-or-nothing unit of work**",
                "Money transfer = {blue:debit} + {green:credit}, together or not at all",
                "Failure midway ==undoes everything== already done"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "BEGIN",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Debit A",
                    "sub": "statement 1",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Credit B",
                    "sub": "statement 2",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "COMMIT",
                    "sub": "or undo all",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Four Guarantees",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Guarantee",
                "Detail"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**A**tomicity",
                  "All apply or none",
                  "Failure midway undoes all"
                ],
                [
                  "**C**onsistency",
                  "Valid state to valid state",
                  "PK, FK, CHECK, UNIQUE never violated"
                ],
                [
                  "**I**solation",
                  "Looks like one at a time",
                  "Only as far as the chosen level allows"
                ],
                [
                  "**D**urability",
                  "Survives crash or power loss",
                  "After COMMIT returns, data is in the log on disk"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Durability Chain",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Write log",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Flush log to disk",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "COMMIT returns",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Isolation is a **dial**, not a guarantee of full serial behaviour: the ==level== you choose decides what other transactions can interfere with."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Commit, Rollback and Savepoints in Practice",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Commit, Rollback and Savepoints in Practice",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Core flow",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "BEGIN",
                    "sub": "open transaction",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Run statements",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "COMMIT",
                    "sub": "make permanent",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ROLLBACK",
                    "sub": "discard all changes",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Transfer: ==both updates== apply together, or neither"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "BEGIN;",
                "UPDATE accounts SET bal = bal - 100 WHERE id = 1;",
                "UPDATE accounts SET bal = bal + 100 WHERE id = 2;",
                "COMMIT;"
              ],
              "note": "debit + credit as one unit"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Autocommit and savepoints",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Autocommit==: each statement is its own transaction",
                "`BEGIN` (`START TRANSACTION`) turns it off until COMMIT/ROLLBACK",
                "`ROLLBACK TO sp1` undoes only work after the ==savepoint==; transaction stays open"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "SAVEPOINT sp1;",
                "-- more statements",
                "ROLLBACK TO sp1;",
                "COMMIT;"
              ],
              "note": "work before sp1 is still committed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Gotchas",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "MySQL",
                "PostgreSQL"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "DDL",
                  "{red:implicit commit}",
                  "{green:transactional DDL}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Postgres error",
              "text": "An error ==aborts the whole transaction==: every statement fails until you `ROLLBACK`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Read Anomalies: Dirty, Non-Repeatable and Phantom",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Read Anomalies: Dirty, Non-Repeatable and Phantom",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three read anomalies",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Anomaly",
                "What you see",
                "Other transaction"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{red:Dirty read}",
                  "uncommitted change, wrong if it rolls back",
                  "not committed yet"
                ],
                [
                  "{orange:Non-repeatable read}",
                  "same row, different value on re-read",
                  "committed an `UPDATE`"
                ],
                [
                  "{purple:Phantom read}",
                  "same range query, different set of rows",
                  "committed an `INSERT` or `DELETE` matching the predicate"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Lost update",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Both transactions read the ==same value==, then both write",
                "One overwrite is {red:silently lost}",
                "Fix: lock the row with `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`, or use one atomic `UPDATE`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "SELECT bal FROM accounts WHERE id = 1 FOR UPDATE;",
                "UPDATE accounts SET bal = bal + 1 WHERE id = 1;"
              ],
              "note": "either form works; the atomic UPDATE needs no prior read"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Write skew",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Two transactions read ==overlapping data==, update **different rows**",
                "Together they break an invariant: two doctors both go off-call",
                "Needs ==SERIALIZABLE== or explicit locking"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Same row or different rows",
              "text": "Lost update hits the **same row**: lock it or use an atomic `UPDATE`. Write skew hits **different rows**: only SERIALIZABLE or explicit locking stops it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Isolation Levels Compared",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Isolation Levels Compared",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The four levels",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Level",
                "Dirty",
                "Non-rep.",
                "Phantom",
                "Default"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "READ UNCOMMITTED",
                  "yes",
                  "yes",
                  "yes",
                  "rarely used"
                ],
                [
                  "READ COMMITTED",
                  "no",
                  "yes",
                  "yes",
                  "PostgreSQL, Oracle, SQL Server"
                ],
                [
                  "REPEATABLE READ",
                  "no",
                  "no",
                  "yes (standard)",
                  "MySQL InnoDB"
                ],
                [
                  "SERIALIZABLE",
                  "no",
                  "no",
                  "no",
                  "none"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. How each one behaves",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==READ COMMITTED==: each statement sees data committed before it started",
                "==REPEATABLE READ==: one snapshot from the first read",
                "InnoDB adds ==gap locks==, blocking most phantoms",
                "==SERIALIZABLE==: outcome equals some serial order, paid in locks or aborts",
                "The app must {red:retry} serialization failures"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Setting the level",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Set it ==per transaction==; the order differs by database, and MySQL gives ERROR 1568 if it is wrong"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "BEGIN;",
                "SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL REPEATABLE READ;"
              ],
              "note": "PostgreSQL: after BEGIN, before the first query"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL REPEATABLE READ;",
                "START TRANSACTION;"
              ],
              "note": "MySQL: before START TRANSACTION, applies to the next one"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Pick the lowest safe level",
              "text": "Higher isolation means ==less concurrency== and more conflicts."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Write-Ahead Logging and Crash Recovery",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Write-Ahead Logging and Crash Recovery",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The WAL Rule",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==WAL rule==: the log record is flushed **before** the data page it describes",
                "{green:COMMIT} needs only the **log flush**, a sequential write",
                "Data pages are written ==lazily== later, so durability is cheap"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Durability chain",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Write log",
                    "note": "change record",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Flush log",
                    "note": "sequential",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Ack COMMIT",
                    "note": "durable",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Write pages",
                    "note": "later",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Steal / No-Force and Checkpoints",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Policy",
                "Dirty page is written",
                "So the log needs"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Steal**",
                  "before commit",
                  "{red:undo}"
                ],
                [
                  "**No-force**",
                  "not forced at commit",
                  "{green:redo}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Checkpoint==: flush dirty pages and record a **log position**",
                "Recovery replays only the log after it, so replay is ==bounded=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. ARIES Recovery: 3 Passes",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Analysis",
                    "sub": "find dirty pages, active txns",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Redo",
                    "sub": "replay logged changes",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Undo",
                    "sub": "roll back uncommitted",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "After a crash",
              "text": "==Redo== committed work, **undo** uncommitted work."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Transactions Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Transactions Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. ACID and Commands",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Atomicity==: all or nothing",
                "==Consistency==: valid state to valid state",
                "==Isolation==: no interference",
                "==Durability==: survives a crash"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "BEGIN;",
                "SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL REPEATABLE READ;",
                "SAVEPOINT x;",
                "ROLLBACK TO x;",
                "COMMIT;  -- or ROLLBACK;"
              ],
              "note": "PostgreSQL order: SET TRANSACTION right after BEGIN"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:MySQL}: `SET TRANSACTION` goes before `START TRANSACTION`; after it, ERROR 1568"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Isolation and Locks",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Level",
                "Non-repeatable",
                "Phantom"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "READ COMMITTED",
                  "{red:allowed}",
                  "{red:allowed}"
                ],
                [
                  "REPEATABLE READ",
                  "{green:prevented}",
                  "{red:allowed} (standard)"
                ],
                [
                  "SERIALIZABLE",
                  "{green:prevented}",
                  "{green:prevented}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` ==locks selected rows==: stops lost updates",
                "Keep transactions ==short==: fewer lock waits and deadlocks"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Durability Chain",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Write log",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Flush log",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Ack COMMIT",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Data pages",
                    "sub": "written later",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "After a crash",
              "text": "==Redo== committed work, ==undo== uncommitted work."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "PostgreSQL, default level. T1 reads a balance (100). T2 sets it to 50 and commits. T1 reads again. What does T1 see?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "50, a non-repeatable read",
                "REPEATABLE READ would still show 100 (snapshot)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Two sessions each read bal (100), then write bal = 110 from the app. What is the final balance, and what is the fix?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "110, so one +10 is lost (lost update)",
                "Use `UPDATE SET bal = bal + 10` or `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "PostgreSQL: BEGIN; INSERT ok; INSERT violates UNIQUE; INSERT ok; COMMIT. What persists?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Nothing",
                "The error aborts the transaction, and later statements fail until ROLLBACK",
                "COMMIT then acts as a ROLLBACK"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "COMMIT returned, then power failed before the data page reached disk. Is the change lost?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No",
                "The log was flushed first (WAL)",
                "Recovery redoes the change from the log"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
